==Gadgets==
===Power Surge===
{{Quote|Surge's power surges! Increase Super charge rate by 30% for 5 sec. Cooldown: 15 seconds.}}{{Gadget|1}}Upon activation, Surge's Super charge rate is increased by 30% for 5 seconds.

{{Quote|Power Surge also grants 30% Reload Speed.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, this Gadget also increases Surge's reload speed by 30%.

===Power Shield===
{{Quote|Within the next 2 seconds, Surge consumes 50% of the damage of the next incoming hit and uses the energy to reload 1 ammo. Cooldown: 22 seconds.}}{{Gadget|2}}When activated, Surge will gain a special shield that lasts for 2 seconds. The next time he takes damage, he only receives 50% of the normal damage and instantly reloads 1 ammo. Unlike [[Nani]]'s Return to Sender Gadget and like [[Kenji]]'s Nigiri Nemesis Star Power, this effect can apply to more than one projectile as long as the damage is done in the same frame (for example, multiple projectiles from [[Shelly]]'s Super). This Gadget's cooldown begins after the button is pressed.

{{Quote|If Surge is hit during Power Shield, Gadget cooldown is decreased by 30%.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, if Surge is hit during the Gadget's activation, the cooldown is decreased by 50%. The reduction is based on the total cooldown, not the remaining cooldown.

==Star Powers==
===To the Max!===
{{Quote|Surge's Main Attack now bounces off walls.}}
{{StarPower|1}}Surge's main attack now also bounces when it hits a wall.

{{Quote|When bouncing off a wall, Surge's Main Attack splits into 2 extra projectiles.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, Surge's main attack also splits into two smaller projectiles when bouncing off a wall. The projectile can split multiple times for multiple bounces off of walls and then again if it hits an enemy Brawler. When Surge's main attack splits on bounce, the split projectiles come out at 30 degree angles instead of 90 degrees.

===Serve Ice Cold===
{{Quote|Surge always spawns with a full Super Charge.}}{{StarPower|2}}When the match starts or Surge respawns after defeat, he will have a fully charged Super. If he had a Super prior to being defeated, it is not affected nor is he given two Supers.

{{Quote|While in Stage 3, Surge gains a burst of movement speed when using his Super.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, after being upgraded to Stage 2+, Surge gains a 50% movement speed boost for 2 seconds after using Super.

==Hypercharge: Juiced Up!==
{{Quote|Surge's Super gains increased ranged and shoots Justice Juice in every direction when landing!}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, when Surge uses his Super, he upgrades to a fourth stage, giving his shots even more range than Stage 2 or 3, and fires 8 smaller attack projectiles around him upon landing. He upgrades to his fourth stage after reaching the third stage, but reverts to Stage 3 after the Hypercharge is over. Additionally, during his Hypercharge's duration, his shots also split regardless if it hits a Brawler or hits a wall with his Star Power To The Max! equipped, even if Surge does not use his Super. Also, his Super jump range is increased by 60%. He also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

{{Quote|Surge shoots 'Double the Juice' for Double the Justice.}}{{Buffie|Hyper}}
With the Buffie, Surge's attack fires two projectiles in quick succession. The second attack projectile deals 50% less damage than the first, and it also charges his Super 50% less. Increased Hypercharge duration by 2 seconds.

